<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Redones</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 56 BCE (approx.) · capital Condate</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Gallic people of eastern Brittany whose chief town Condate became the city of Rennes.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Redones lived in the basin of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vilaine">Vilaine</a>, in the modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ille-et-vilaine">Ille-et-Vilaine</a>. Caesar lists them among the Armorican peoples who submitted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/publius-licinius-crassus">Publius Crassus</a> in 57 BCE.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Their oppidum of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rennes">Condate</a> stood at the confluence of the Ille and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vilaine">Vilaine</a>, as its Gaulish name, meaning confluence, indicates. They struck gold coins of Armorican type.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>They sent troops to relieve <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-alesia">Alesia</a> in 52 BCE. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rennes">Condate</a> became a walled civitas capital, called Redones in late antiquity, the origin of Rennes, later the capital of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-brittany">Duchy of Brittany</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/redones.jpg" alt="Redones" width="320" height="161"><figcaption>Image: cgb · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stat%C3%A8re_de_billon_frapp%C3%A9_par_les_Riedones.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 56 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Condate</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gaulish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-178&amp;focus=redones" aria-label="Redones on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4818 559 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Redones lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5138 815L5304 942"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5138 815h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5138 815h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Condate. <a href="/atlas?year=-178&amp;focus=redones">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

